---
import StoreBadges from '../components/StoreBadges.astro';
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is Recur similar to BodBot?',
    answer:
      "Both take joint and injury issues seriously. BodBot markets itself around 'taking control of your joints.' Recur doesn't ask you to set up a separate injury profile. You flag what's bothering you as you go, and it adjusts from there.",
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title="Recur vs BodBot | Recur"
  description="How Recur compares to BodBot: pain routing, free tier, and everyday simplicity."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: faq.question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer },
    })),
  })} />

  <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2">Recur vs BodBot</h1>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-12">A straight comparison, not a sales pitch.</p>

  <div class="max-w-none space-y-10 text-foreground">
    <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      BodBot markets itself as a digital personal trainer built around "taking control of your
      joints," which puts it closest to Recur's own focus on training around pain. Here's where
      the two actually differ.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Where Recur is different</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Three workouts a week are free, forever. Not a trial.</li>
        <li>No separate injury setup. Flag a knee or shoulder mid-flow and Recur routes around it from your next session on.</li>
        <li>Take a few weeks off and Recur eases you back in instead of resuming at your old volume.</li>
        <li>Built specifically for home equipment: dumbbells, kettlebells, bodyweight.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">What's similar</h2>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Both apps treat training around pain as a first-class feature instead of an afterthought.
        If that's the reason you're looking at BodBot, it's worth trying Recur's free tier before
        you decide.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">FAQ</h2>
      {faqs.map(faq => (
        <div class="mb-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">{faq.question}</h3>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="pt-6">
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Three workouts a week, free, forever. See for yourself.
      </p>
      <StoreBadges location="vs_bodbot_page" />
    </section>
  </div>
</ContentPage>
